WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.033
-Our next guest stars
in the comedy special

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:07.167
"Entre Nos: The Winners 3,"
available now on HBO Max.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.901
Making his late-night debut,
please welcome the very funny

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.901
Ralph Barbosa.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.267
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:26.033
It is such an honor to be here
making my late-night debut.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.868
Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.367
Especially because my
grandmother, who raised me,

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.033
she's a huge fan of comedy.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.234
If you would have told her
that, one day, I'd be here on

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.067
"The Tonight Show
with Jimmy Fallon,"

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.767
she probably
would have said, "Qué?"

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:40.400
Because she
doesn't know English.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.367
I love living at my grandma's.

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:48.334
When you're being raised by
an old woman

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:53.501
who doesn't speak English, you
grow up with zero consequences.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:56.033
Like, I used to get
phone calls from school.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:59.434
But who do you think she needed
to translate these calls?

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:04.167
That's right. I ran that house.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:07.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.801
Anytime anybody called
the house speaking English,

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.267
she'd put the house phone
on speaker

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.300
and she would be like,
"Who is it?

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.367
What are they saying?"

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.067
And I'd act like
I'm listening real hard

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.234
and I would be like,

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:21.934
"Man, Grandma,
they're talking really fast.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.100
It's kind of hard to understand,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.801
but they're saying
something about...

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:29.033
p-proof of residency?"

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:31.467
She's like, "Hang up."
I'm like, "If you say so."

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.300
I lived with my mom for a while,
too, and she was cool.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.133
She never really kept
my dad around,

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:45.567
but she always kept
father figures around.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.367
I actually ran into my mom's
ex-boyfriend the other day.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:49.868
He's doing really good.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:53.601
He was right --
we were holding him back.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:55.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.267
He has a car now.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.334
I approached him. I had to.

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.901
I was like, "Dude,
if this is what getting away

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:09.701
from my mom looks like,
I'm ready, man."

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:14.467
I recently became a father.
I have a beautiful baby boy.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.968
Mm-hmm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.734
Thank you.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.033
Yeah, it's great.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:22.601
But it's also very scary
having a baby at a young age.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.534
I feel like I'm a new employee

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:29.400
who just got put to train
an even newer employee.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.801
'Cause I just
look at my son like,

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:35.667
"I don't -- I haven't been
here that long, man."

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.000
I could show you where we eat.
That's about it."

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.701
But it is amazing watching him
learn things and grow.

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.634
Like, he's walking now.
He knows how to ask for food.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:03:00.400
I was like, "Dang.
I've taught you all I can, son.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.133
From here on out,
we learn together."

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.567
I like buying him
lots of sneakers,

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:06.868
'cause I'm big on sneakers.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.267
Last month,
I went a little crazy.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.834
I bought us like
eight pairs of shoes --

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.934
four for me,
four for my baby boy.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.968
He doesn't fit into
a size 9 yet,

00:03:13.968 --> 00:03:16.000
so I wear his half
for now, but...

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.601
I love being a dad.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.701
He does embarrass me
sometimes in public.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.167
Like, we go to the mall
together a lot,

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.834
and he'll be walking next to me.

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:30.100
And he stares at everybody
we walk past.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.334
And whenever he sees
a really pretty girl,

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.467
he'll let go of my hand,
walk up to the girl,

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.634
and ask her to carry him.

00:03:36.634 --> 00:03:39.033
And I have to be like,
"Hey, I'm so sorry about that.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:42.567
I think my son just wants us
to go out for drinks."

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:46.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.634
I recently moved out from home
for the first time ever.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.300
I got my first apartment.

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:57.501
Yeah. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.501 --> 00:04:00.367
It's a small apartment,
but I love it.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:01.501
I'm very proud of it.

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:02.734
I've been trying to show it off,

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:05.734
mostly to get girls
to notice me.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:10.300
Like, everywhere I go,
I take my lease with me now

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.701
and just let it hang out
my pocket a little bit.

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.067
The other day, I acted like

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.501
I accidentally dropped it
by a girl.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:16.868
She picked it up.

00:04:16.868 --> 00:04:18.934
She was like, "Hey, you dropped
this piece of paper."

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:23.200
I was like, "Oh, man,
did I drop my 13-month lease?"

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.300
It was like, "You keep that.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.868
That's you right there."

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.968
Now, to be 100% honest,
I do want the apartment

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:34.601
to get girls to notice me,
but after that deposit

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.968
and that one furniture I bought,

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:41.033
I don't really have
money left for dating.

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:43.033
Like, I've approached
one girl at a bar.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.133
I was like, "Hey, what's up?
What are you drinking?"

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.367
And she was like,
"A Crown and Coke."

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:49.467
I was like, "Nice."

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:56.667
And that was as far as
I could afford to go.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:59.367
But then I told myself,
"I shouldn't overthink it."

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.467
So, I was like, "You know what?
I'mma go for it."

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.567
And I said...

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:06.934
"Could you buy
me one, too, please?"

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:09.601
I'm Ralph Barbosa.
Thank you guys so much.

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:13.767
-That's how
you do it right there.

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:14.868
That's how you do it.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.067
Ralph Barbosa!

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:23.033
"Entre Nos: The Winners 3"
is available now on HBO Max.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.467
We'll be right back, everybody.
Ralph Barbosa.

